/// §7.1's remap, applied once to an already-aggregated severity (§C.7's `infer_severity`),
/// not per-commit — see the SPEC DECISION below for why that is equivalent and simpler.
///
/// Gate (both conditions independently make this inert, per §7.1's exact wording: "Inert…
/// when the current version is `0.0.z` or there is no prior tag"):
/// - `has_prior_release == false` → inert unconditionally. A package with no release history
///   has nothing to be "pre-major" *relative to* in the sense this setting means; treating a
///   freshly-scaffolded package's first-ever inference as remappable would let the setting
///   fire on a version number that is not really a release line yet.
/// - `current_version` is `0.0.z` (major == 0 **and** minor == 0) → inert. This exact
///   boundary is called out in §7.1 as where release-please's `bumpMinorPreMajor` leaked bugs
///   (its issues #2087/#2635), so it is a named, tested case here rather than an emergent one.
/// - Otherwise (`0.y.z`, `y > 0`, prior release exists) → the gate is open; `breaking_to_minor`
///   and `feat_to_patch` each apply independently if set.
/// - A version with `major > 0` is not pre-major at all and is always inert.
///
/// Returns `(final_severity, remapped)` — `remapped` is `true` iff the returned severity
/// differs from `raw`, matching `BumpReason::Inference.remapped`'s exact meaning (§M.12.3).
/// `Severity::None`/`Severity::Patch` inputs are always returned unchanged — this policy only
/// ever maps `Major → Minor` and `Minor → Patch`.
pub fn apply_pre_major_policy(
    raw: Severity,
    policy: &PreMajorInferencePolicy,
    current_version: &Version,
    has_prior_release: bool,
) -> (Severity, bool);
